  "worked_solution": "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-8)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=2$ and $k=8.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(2,8).$",
